  "reason": "Evidence: config_010 (multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, weighted) achieved 0.639 accuracy, a large jump over config_007's 0.523 (singleprofile), confirming multiprofile+avgpool is the dominant design choice. Uncertainty: whether the weighted fusion is optimal or whether concatenation captures complementary modality information more effectively. This experiment tests exactly that—config_008 is identical to config_010 except fusion changes from weighted to concat. It is the minimal, most informative single-variable change from the current best, directly clarifying whether we can push accuracy higher with a different fusion strategy before investing in more expensive encoder or aggregation changes. Expected relative cost: similar to config_010 (~10–11 GPU hours) since the architecture (multiprofile, resnet50, avgpool) is unchanged; only the fusion layer differs, so training time should be comparable."
}

